<blockquote class="uncited"><div>You mean, you usually copy the dlls?<br>Since bullet usually comes as a static build (i.e., .lib files) you have to tell him to use these libs (which, by the way, you still would need for interfaces in the dll builds)<br><br>To link libraries in VC8, open the project properties, and go to the linker settings.<br>There, in the "General" tab, add the path to your bullet libraries to the item called "Additional Library Directories"; which beforehand you should all copy to one directory, to make things easier.<br>Finally, go to the "input" tab, and add all required bullet libraries to the "additional dependencies" list.<br><br>Hope this helps</div></blockquote>Still the same, although it is successfully build and run, using the demo.<br><br>The funny thing is that I create my HelloWorld Project from scratch, with the whole part of the code is copy-pasted. But, when it is run, it prompts "Unhandled exception at 0x0045f81d in HelloWorld.exe: 0xC0000005: Access violation reading location 0x5b845c33."<br><br>Is that anything I need to do to build my own project from scratch?? (Besides, linking all of the dependencies and libraries)<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=5093">1245TA</a> — Tue May 05, 2009 4:33 am</p><hr />
