You mean, you usually copy the dlls?<br>Since bullet usually comes as a static build (i.e., .lib files) you have to tell him to use these libs (which, by the way, you still would need for interfaces in the dll builds)<br><br>To link libraries in VC8, open the project properties, and go to the linker settings.<br>There, in the "General" tab, add the path to your bullet libraries to the item called "Additional Library Directories"; which beforehand you should all copy to one directory, to make things easier.<br>Finally, go to the "input" tab, and add all required bullet libraries to the "additional dependencies" list.<br><br>Hope this helps<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=3001">Dominik</a> — Mon May 04, 2009 5:41 pm</p><hr />
